{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller","id":1161628,"title":"Questions about abuse - Beginner Storyteller","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-22T15:32:01-08:00","id":1161628,"title":"Questions about abuse - Beginner Storyteller","content":"So, I write this because a friend of mine is having trouble in a game of his. I tried helping him, but I learned with the 3ed and he is using the m20 and one of his players is quite the powergamer. I'd like help with a few rules<br /> <br /> 1-) Sanctum background. The player just put the cult background and sanctum plus wonder(prime 5) at maximum, so he'd stock up quintessence and always reduce the difficulty of magics inside the sanctum. With this, he is making effects with 50 successes or more. Now, in 3ed when the effect came out of the sanctum, it instantly was undone. There is nothing like this when we searched m20. We asked in some forums, and people told us to use the unbelief rule. But there are some problems<br /> A-) the player is making the pattern alteration that he causes stronger with quintessence, making it harder to dissolve trough unbelief<br /> B-) The unbelief rule is vague, at best.<br /> 2-) There is no rule for permanent paradox in regards to creating armos with the life sphere, claws and so on. The player is doing just that. He made an armor with 50 successes with life 3. And some other colorful things. We are well aware of the rule about permanente paradox in regards to attributes, but there is just that. Nothing in regards to changing soaking(Like there was in verbena 3ed) and so on<br /> 3-) The storyteller does not use the resonance rule because it is optional. We used ressonance in 3ed to limit getting quintessence with prime. After some time, it made you a beacon of supernatural energy. But since the ressonance rule is optional, how to deal with this?<br /> <br /> What is my friend, the storyteller from that game, missing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:09:42-08:00","id":1161672,"title":"","content":"A few possibilities come to mind.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Permanent Paradox</u></b><br /> <br /> Depending on whether they are making the changes to themselves or an object Permanent Paradox might occur (bolded for emphasis) pg 548<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Permanent Paradox generally comes through the Enhancement Background Trait, described in Chapter Six. Severe backlashes bestow such points as well, and<b> certain alterations to a creature\u2019s Pattern may do so too.</b> Bygones and constructs often suffer from permanent Paradox points \u2013 a flaw that keeps certain Technocracy operatives or Nephandi confined to the Otherworlds. (See the HIT Marks in Appendix I and the Gilledians described in Chapter Five.) Essentially, a being with permanent Paradox is a walking reality crime \u2013 a violation of Earthly metaphysics whose own body is hazardous to her health. </div> </div> </div>In the wonders section there is a spot about permanent Paradox and items pg 652<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Permanent Paradox<br /> On the flipside, certain Wonders ripple the Consensus simply by existing. The Enhancement Background (described in Chapter Six) invokes that kind of permanent Paradox, and<b> certain other things do as well. For the most part, permanent Paradox comes about through certain lasting modifications: moving tattoos, glowing horns, and the like. In general, assume that a Wonder that can be turned off or set aside does not generate permanent Paradox. If a Wonder does involve permanent Paradox, add that Paradox to the wielder\u2019s Quintessence/ Paradox wheel whenever he has that Wonder in his possession</b>. </div> </div> </div>So the character's super armor is clearly stronger than any terrestrial material and thus could fall afoul of having Permanent Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Limiting Successes for Some Effects</u></b><br /> <br /> Below the chart on base damage and duration (pg 504) has the following suggestion<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To preserve game balance, the Storyteller may choose to cap damage at 20 health levels (10 successes, or nine successes for Forces Sphere attacks). </div> </div> </div>This same idea could be used for effects that soak damage.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Quiet</u></b><br /> <br /> Blatantly ignoring reality's boundaries repeatedly (such as making personal armor that is sturdier than mountains) could result in the Mage developing Quiet as they lose their grip on what things are supposed to be. pg 554<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Storyteller makes some plans, based around a particular character\u2019s personality <b>and actions</b>, and decides how this particular case of Quiet will manifest. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>When the character reaches a particular goal</b> (say, 10 Paradox points), or endures a certain challenge to her sanity (reading a blasphemous tome, perhaps), the Storyteller begins slipping notes to the player, describing the delusions or suggesting irrational acts. </div> </div> </div><u><b>The Enemy</b></u><br /> <br /> If the character had the idea its quite possible that the enemy (Technocrats, Nephandi, etc) have had the same idea. So he might have his super armor, but the Technocrats break out a high powered turbolaser to deal with it. Additionally such potent effects could very easily stand out to Awakened sense, at that number of successes possibly even Awareness might pick up on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:53:41-08:00","id":1161695,"title":"","content":"Now, I'm very thankful for your reply, and I'm sure it will help. If other members could colaborate as well, it would be nice.<br /> I gotta say, tough, the friend I'm helping wouldn't like to create a houserule to solve this, based on the rules that are in the book. He would like to use something that objectively deals with the situation. I'm worried there isn't - altough your answer is very much appreciated nonetheless, as well as the time you took to help us =)!<br /> We tried using the rule that limited successes and the rule that sets a time for rituals(Great work) but it didn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:55:10-08:00","id":1161699,"title":"","content":"Because you are dealing with such an outlier case of using various rules in conjunction there is no definitive way. That is kind of how Mage is, the ST needs to do some adjudication because Mages can do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T19:01:27-08:00","id":1161701,"title":"","content":"Ya, I feel that. Altough when I used to be a storyteller in the 3ed I didn't have so much problems as my friend did. I used to limit successes in arete+Willpower. I guess that is why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T20:05:16-08:00","id":1161726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schrodingoethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller?p=1161701#post1161701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya, I feel that. Altough when I used to be a storyteller in the 3ed I didn't have so much problems as my friend did. I used to limit successes in arete+Willpower. I guess that is why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, now that's how many rolls you can make.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly my solution is simple. Inform the player that Min/Maxing and powergaming isn't the type of game your running and if they don't like that then they should find another ST.<br /> <br /> I realize that isn't feasible for everyone unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T20:26:57-08:00","id":1161733,"title":"","content":"My friend was surely thinking about it. But he wanted to find an alternative solution, so we tried posting here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T20:53:27-08:00","id":1161743,"title":"","content":"Of the options I suggested I think either Permanent Paradox and/or Limited Successes are the best. They limit opponents as much as himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T20:56:23-08:00","id":1161744,"title":"","content":"Indeed. My friend and I were thinking about the Unbelief rule as well and ways to develop it a bit more. I used to think the best option was to limit the amount of successes per effect. Like.. arete+Willpower. That used to work in 3ed - it was pretty nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T22:06:05-08:00","id":1161756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schrodingoethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller#post1161628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I write this because a friend of mine is having trouble in a game of his. I tried helping him, but I learned with the 3ed and he is using the m20 and one of his players is quite the powergamer. I'd like help with a few rules<br /> <br /> 1-) Sanctum background. The player just put the cult background and sanctum plus wonder(prime 5) at maximum, so he'd stock up quintessence and always reduce the difficulty of magics inside the sanctum. With this, he is making effects with 50 successes or more. Now, in 3ed when the effect came out of the sanctum, it instantly was undone. There is nothing like this when we searched m20. We asked in some forums, and people told us to use the unbelief rule. But there are some problems<br /> A-) the player is making the pattern alteration that he causes stronger with quintessence, making it harder to dissolve trough unbelief<br /> B-) The unbelief rule is vague, at best.<br /> 2-) There is no rule for permanent paradox in regards to creating armos with the life sphere, claws and so on. The player is doing just that. He made an armor with 50 successes with life 3. And some other colorful things. We are well aware of the rule about permanente paradox in regards to attributes, but there is just that. Nothing in regards to changing soaking(Like there was in verbena 3ed) and so on<br /> 3-) The storyteller does not use the resonance rule because it is optional. We used ressonance in 3ed to limit getting quintessence with prime. After some time, it made you a beacon of supernatural energy. But since the ressonance rule is optional, how to deal with this?<br /> <br /> What is my friend, the storyteller from that game, missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need some things clarified:<br /> <br /> From the context it seems that this Chronicle has been going on for quite some time. Characters with Prime 5 are not possible under the normal character creation rules. At this point he is a Master, and should be capable of truly amazing feats. However, I could be interpreting this incorrectly and the Wonder is what is giving him access to all of this Quintessence. What specifically does the Wonder do? At 5 dots it probably has a few powers, but it should definitely have limits to what it is capable of. Wonders don't get access to the entire list of Sphere effects, just some specific rotes.<br /> <br /> How is he maintaining his cult? He's performing some spectacular effects with their assistance. He's bound to get the attention of folks who look down on that type of thing. Technocrats and Hitmarks could pay him a visit. <br /> <br /> Sanctum only makes the casting of an effect coincidental. Breaking the boundaries of what is plausible within reality will still garner Paradox on effects that are removed outside that little reality zone. Permanent paradox points, pattern bleeding, Quiets, etc. Why not use this as a great moment to highlight the theme of hubris in Mage and make him go into a quiet or be taken into a paradox realm by an angry paradox spirit?<br /> <br /> Pattern bleeding deals with permanent modifications that are not paid for with XP. As ST I'd make him purchase the body modifications using the Enhancement background as a guideline. This gives him the choice of Patten bleeding or permadox.<br /> <br /> Finally, at a certain point the number of successes achieved on an effect cease to matter, or you must use a higher Sphere rank to do so. A Life 3 effect is only every going to do something within the realm of possibility for Life 3. 20 successes or 50 successes, it doesn't matter. I'd cap the armor gained at 10 points and make the duration permanent unless unwoven. You can't make yourself immune to all damage with life 3 no matter how many dice you roll. <br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds like there may be some miscommunication between the player and the ST on their expectations from the game, and some misunderstandings of the rules and the role the ST plays as arbiter of those rules. The ST needs to talk with the player and make sure that it's understood that this behavior is clearly taking advantage of the system and the ST, and it needs to stop in the name of fun and for the sake of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T22:25:26-08:00","id":1161760,"title":"","content":"My friend has been talking with him, no doubt. The player is quite hot-headed, tough, so, we'll probably take him off the game. In any case, my friend dislikes houseruling his game - and that was the reason we ended up in such a situation. Now, to clarify things..<br /> 1-) The quintessence comes from the wonder, which has an effect of prime 5 that lets him draw quintessence from anywhere, as stated in the sphere.<br /> The rest of your advice is pretty solid, but before using the scenario against the player we decided to at least come here and see if there were rules that we were missing. Your idea about the life sphere is very good as well.<br /> The player solves pattern bleeding with quintessence - which he has unlimited, really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T02:31:34-08:00","id":1161799,"title":"","content":"Just a thought here - but has your friend considered the rule for rituals involving brief rites, ceremonies, and great works (pg 541)? This kind of thing will make spells with 50 successes incredibly hard to achieve, limiting folks to 1-10 successes depending on their stamina capabilities.<br /> <br /> If that's not enough, it's also worth noting that while Sanctum does make the effects of a mage's powers coincidental, that's _only within the confines of reality within that location_. It's essentially a minor reality zone, usually attuned to the mage in question. Why this is important, is because it means that the mage will not be breaking any of the Foundations of the reality - and yes, some effects will still be vulgar. In no paradigm is your skin being able to shrug off a nuke without a scratch coincidental, and while you might be able to convince a cult that you are able to armor him up or what have you, some things will be beyond their belief. (...Also, some things will be beyond their <i>time</i>. Cultists are people too - if he abuses them and only uses them to benefit himself, that merit will dwindle.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T05:45:28-08:00","id":1161836,"title":"","content":"We already use the great work rule. And nah, it didn't work. The character makes himself do not need sleep or respite using life magic.<br /> The problem with sanctum, as mentioned, is that, basically that, once the effect is done, and it is taken outside, there is no paradox attributed to it. That was the biggest problem with that idea until now.<br /> He does treat his cult well, tough. But the storyteller didn't want to use the scenario against him until we checked the rules and saw that we weren't missing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T06:27:17-08:00","id":1161840,"title":"","content":"Hmmm....<br /> <br /> I didn't notice any Avatar background mentioned there. That could be a problem for one. And the Wonder lets the character draw in quint from the universe, great, but where is he storing it? It's a separate use of Prime to utilize Tass an without an Avatar background he's going to struggle storing it in his pattern/using that quint for anything.<br /> <br /> No sleep nor respite is asking for pattern bleed as is if he's just making it so he can soak unearthly levels of harm.<br /> Armour with the Life Sphere? So he's either Increased his Physical Attributes OR he's wearing a created life form with Increased Physical Attributes (to whit Stamina) that he's also having to spend successes on to be able to soak lethal and maybe even Aggravated damage (both of which tend to come across as Vulgar when they are used, not cast and can also cause Bleed or Quiet). Plus there's the time taken to do this, what is the rest of the cabal up to while he's taking all this time to generate 50 successes? There's around probably around 20hrs of casting time there for an Arete 3 character (without knowing the paradigm), unless he's using magick to also make his cult immune to tiredness, distraction and food (which would also require the Mind sphere). If so then you have things like Domino Effect, or penalties for maintaining additional Magickal Effects.<br /> <br /> The key problem though is seemingly the unwillingness of the ST to rule on these things, it's not even House Ruling but Mage requires the ST to take the examples of how things like Paradox, Pattern Bleed and Quiet function and apply them to a characters actions. You wont get a hard and fast on a lot of that because of the sheer scope and flexibility of the Magick that Mage uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","user":"Moirdryd","date":". 11-23-2017, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T06:31:00-08:00","id":1161842,"title":"","content":"Can't you still get Paradox from a botch in a sanctum? And don't two botches always cut short extended Arete rolls? I don't see how anyone gets 50 successes on an Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T06:47:42-08:00","id":1161845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller?p=1161842#post1161842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you still get Paradox from a botch in a sanctum? And don't two botches always cut short extended Arete rolls? I don't see how anyone gets 50 successes on an Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's feasible. You get 5 extra successes each roll using the Cult (if maxed), With that much backup you can get there in less than 10 rolls. I would think that you can do 8-9 rolls without botching with low difficulties, a little luck, and Willpower. Of course, that's still a lot of effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T07:28:19-08:00","id":1161856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schrodingoethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller?p=1161836#post1161836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already use the great work rule. And nah, it didn't work. The character makes himself do not need sleep or respite using life magic.<br /> The problem with sanctum, as mentioned, is that, basically that, once the effect is done, and it is taken outside, there is no paradox attributed to it. That was the biggest problem with that idea until now.<br /> He does treat his cult well, tough. But the storyteller didn't want to use the scenario against him until we checked the rules and saw that we weren't missing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the scenary it's your friend...<br /> <br /> It's not a bad time to remember the good old times of revised where a Sanctum didn't work like this: <i>&quot;once the effect is done, and it is taken outside, there is no paradox attributed to it&quot;</i>.<br /> In Revised when you cast an effect in a Sanctum that would otherwise be vulgar, you can't take the effect out of the Sanctum because such effect vanishes from Unbelief at the moment you went out. You needed to cast your effect as Vulgar to make it work outside. Or so was implied in the Guide to the Traditions. Now, that was a good ruling, I think, consistent with the Setting. If your friend was thinking on developing Unbelief, that's a good place to start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like.. arete+Willpower. That used to work in 3ed - it was pretty nice. </div> </div> </div>I'm almost sure that in revised basic the limit was stated to be the product of Arete and Willpower, that would be Arete x Willpower. Also the book stated that to calculate this you shouldn't include the successes of asistants or acolites because a mage with a lot of followers should be able to do impressive stuff (meaning that 50 successes can be reached with the Cult). p. 150<br /> <br /> Perhaps you were &quot;house ruling&quot; all along? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T08:13:46-08:00","id":1161870,"title":"","content":"he gets 50 successes using the cult and with low difficulties. He indeed has a avatar rating, altough I didn't mentioned it. The group helps him store quintessence, from time to time. Normally, tough, he just gets it inside the sanctum before doing an effect. He isn't needing even that much quintessence, tbh. Just enough to reinforce the pattern so it doesn't dissolves when hit with the unbelief rule.<br /> He fights pattern bleeding with quintessence, really. The cult does indeed gets tired after a while. They don't help so much in the ritual, most of them go away and so on. But it is still enough to get a load of successes, lol.That the storyteller really did in the chronicle.<br /> I didn't understand something you posted, Moirdryd, do I get paradox only when I use the alteration? Where do I find this rule?<br /> Wholeheartedly agree with you, tough, the system works much better with storyteller handling things directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T08:15:19-08:00","id":1161871,"title":"","content":"Ah, don't take me wrong, aleph, the arete+willpower was my houserule. As a storyteller I've no problem doing that. My friend dislikes it tough. Great hugh =P!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T08:21:29-08:00","id":1161874,"title":"","content":"I also had the same idea as you, Aleph, I liked the rule in 3ed for sanctum much, much more. Was talking about that in the past posts.. it certainly would serve well to help with the unbelief rule, as you said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T12:57:09-08:00","id":1161943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller?p=1161845#post1161845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's feasible. You get 5 extra successes each roll using the Cult (if maxed), With that much backup you can get there in less than 10 rolls. I would think that you can do 8-9 rolls without botching with low difficulties, a little luck, and Willpower. Of course, that's still a lot of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you can get extra dice not successes, but still it can add up quiickly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:23:11-08:00","id":1161951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schrodingoethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161628-questions-about-abuse-beginner-storyteller?p=1161836#post1161836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already use the great work rule. And nah, it didn't work. The character makes himself do not need sleep or respite using life magic.<br /> The problem with sanctum, as mentioned, is that, basically that, once the effect is done, and it is taken outside, there is no paradox attributed to it. That was the biggest problem with that idea until now.<br /> He does treat his cult well, tough. But the storyteller didn't want to use the scenario against him until we checked the rules and saw that we weren't missing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes - but is he doing that for the entire cult? The thing about this that seems a bit wonky to me is that at that point, your having an entire group of people stay up doing the same things for hours, sometimes days before you manage to finish a single spell. If this is done maybe once a month, or once a year, I can see that being a thing - but your regularly scheduled great rite is going to strain folks psychologically - unless, of course, he's including those folks in the casting and helping them personally with their lives (blessing them with luck, applying thirty of those 50 successes on armor to the cultists themselves, etc.)<br /> <br /> I don't have much for the Sanctum thing. Far as I recalled, if someone realized an effect was vulgar after they saw it was coincidental, it blew up as a vulgar effect and dissipated completely. That may be a different edition though as I can't seem to find it. *Reads up before posting this* Apparently its revised.<br /> <br /> That said - that doesn't sound like treating the cult well - if you are abusing the backgrounds, remember that the cultist are people - 30 different people, who they themselves can feel abused or used. Let's face the facts, if folks are regularly being called away to these rites (I'm assuming this is not an infrequent thing?) and are spending days casting these spells, they are going to attract attention in their daily lives. The cultists have lives you know, beyond the mage. They are people - usually in an industrial area where you need to maintain a job in order to survive.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, they have the 'power dissipates and backlash hits anyways' rule when describing illusions in How Do You DO That... which points out that it's coincidental, until it's proven vulgar, and then gives the illusion two options for what happened. I would use those rules for spells cast in a Sanctum that leave a Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 11-23-2017, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:29:15-08:00","id":1161952,"title":"","content":"Ah, Jakondite, it is far from that. Until now, he has done this only 3-4 times in some 5 months. The storyteller dealth a bit with time skiping, and that is true. He does give money, food and treats his cult as his own children. He just asks them to perform these things from time to time. Also, the cult doesn't stick around for the entire spell - I think I mentioned that somewhere. And aye, that rule is from revised. Thanks for trying to help anyway! =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:20:55-08:00","id":1162306,"title":"","content":"Well, first of your friend really need to revisit this &quot;don't house-rule&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Not because I think it is important or such on a general manner, but because M20 was specifically built that way. It is vague on some critical rules because it is meant to be fine-tuned for your chronicle, and be receptive for rules from previous editions. At least your friend <u>should</u> choose a previous edition to rule on such stuff, or he isn't actually using the rules on M20.<br /> <br /> Second, your friend could just look at it from out-of-the-box. Think about real life, and then think about someone just hiring a mad soldier as a body guard and arming the soldier with a sub-machine gun. Think about everything this person will have to deal with just because of it (and yeah, it isn't impossible to do). How the world at large see the PC? How people react? An extremely powerful character that stays out of trouble and plays with the group isn't actually that of a problem. But if this character is a trouble for people around, then those people will find a way to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Given, a character that pretty much became a threat on the level of a Master can easily attract the actual attention of a Master. Sanctums can be targeted by enemies. A character that heavily relies on a few resources can have those very resources targeted. Instead of thinking on how to rule out the advantages, let the NPCs do the hard work with everything they have.<br /> <br /> And if in the end it isn't possible to have fun with this guy, then get rid of the player altogether. The game is about everyone having a good time, and if a member needs to deny fun to other, they simply can't play together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T21:09:13-08:00","id":1162344,"title":"","content":"That is all true, Indeed. My friend decided to use the rule about sanctum from 3ed now. It is working quite well. He still has trouble when the player works outside his sanctum, but at least we acomplished something. The player also seems to be getting out of the table little by little. He is missing sessions and so on. My friend didn't even got the chance to talk to him. Thanks to those who helped =_)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}